  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target community for this meme is individuals who are familiar with or have a casual understanding of World War II history, particularly the Holocaust, and who may find humor in absurd or exaggerated analogies. The meme likely appeals to an audience that enjoys dark humor, shock value, or satirical comparisons, especially those who are not deeply sensitive to historical trauma. It may also target those who are part of online communities that engage in meme culture, where historical figures are often used for comedic effect, even if it trivializes serious events. The meme’s use of beauty and personal care as a metaphor suggests it may also resonate with individuals in the beauty industry or those who identify with cosmetic routines, as it plays on the idea of trivializing beauty-related acts. However, the meme’s harmful intent and historical trivialization make it offensive to many, particularly survivors and descendants of Holocaust victims, and thus its target audience may be unintentionally excluding or alienating those communities.",
